# Tauri – Vertical Slices

Business logic lives in `src-tauri/src/slices/<slice>/`.

## Slice contents

Typical per slice:

- `mod.rs` – public slice API
- `commands.rs` – Tauri commands
- Keep slice domain/persistence code local to the slice

## Rules

- `lib.rs` only wires plugins, state, and command registration
- No cross-slice domain logic in `lib.rs`
- Slices communicate through clear APIs, not internals
- Host/local network serving is its own slice (e.g. `network`), not frontend code
- Frontend must call Tauri only through `src/shared/api` facades

## Example

```rust
// lib.rs – wiring only
.invoke_handler(tauri::generate_handler![
    slices::greet::commands::greet,
])
```
